> Run commands based on what an entity is looking at.

name View
slug bookshelf-view
version 5.0.0
tags runtime

$run: #[command(slash="forbidden",empty="forbidden")] string
$provider: #[id(registry="function",tags="allowed")] string
$aimed: $provider > [block provider](hitbox.md#block-providers) of the blocks that stop the view, `#bs.hitbox:get_block/outline` by default
$max_distance: number @ 0..2047 > distance the entity sees at most, 16 by default

$target: struct
  blocks?: $aimed
  entities?: $provider > [entity provider](hitbox.md#entity-providers) of the entities that stop the view, `#bs.hitbox:get_entity/targetable` by default
  selector?: string > selector arguments the entities must match, such as `tag=my_pack.target`
  max_distance?: $max_distance


feature function at_aimed_block > Run a command as an entity, at the block it aims at.
  authors Aksiome
  since 2023/11/30 1.20.3
  @executor > entity that looks, from its eyes
  input arguments
    run: $run > command to run as the entity, at the block, aligned to the grid
    blocks?: $aimed
    max_distance?: $max_distance
  output success > whether the entity aims at a block

feature function as_aimed_entity > Run a command as and at the entity an entity aims at.
  authors Aksiome
  since 2023/11/30 1.20.3
  @executor > entity that looks, from its eyes
  input arguments
    run: $run > command to run as and at the aimed entity
    $target
  output success > whether the entity aims at an entity

feature function at_aimed_entity > Run a command as an entity, at the entity it aims at.
  authors Aksiome
  since 2023/11/30 1.20.3
  @executor > entity that looks, from its eyes
  input arguments
    run: $run > command to run as the entity that aims, at the aimed entity
    $target
  output success > whether the entity aims at an entity

feature function at_aimed_point > Run a command as an entity, at the point where its view hits a block or an entity.
  authors Aksiome
  since 2024/01/25 1.20.3
  @executor > entity that looks, from its eyes
  input arguments
    run: $run > command to run as the entity, at the point
    $target
  output success > whether the entity aims at a block or an entity

feature function at_block_placement > Run a command as an entity, where a block it places would go: against the face of the block it aims at.
  authors Aksiome
  since 2024/01/24 1.20.4
  @executor > entity that looks, from its eyes
  input arguments
    run: $run > command to run as the entity, at the block where a block would be placed, aligned to the grid
    blocks?: $provider > [block provider](hitbox.md#block-providers) of the blocks to place against, `#bs.hitbox:get_block/interaction` by default
    max_distance?: $max_distance
  output success > whether the entity aims at a block

feature function as_looked_entity > Run a command as the entity a player looks at, where the function runs. Only entities tagged `bs.view.is_lookable` can be looked at.
  authors Aksiome
  since 2023/12/06 1.20.3
  @executor > player that looks
  output result > result of the command
  output success > whether the player looks at an entity
  input arguments
    run: $run > command to run as the looked entity, at the position of the function

feature function at_looked_entity > Run a command as a player, at the entity it looks at. Only entities tagged `bs.view.is_lookable` can be looked at.
  authors Aksiome
  since 2023/12/06 1.20.3
  @executor > player that looks
  output result > result of the command
  output success > whether the player looks at an entity
  input arguments
    run: $run > command to run as the player, at the looked entity

feature function can_see > Check if an entity can see a position: no block stands between its eyes and the position.
  authors Aksiome, Leirof
  since 2019/05/20 1.20.3
  @executor > entity that looks, from its eyes
  @position > position to see
  input arguments
    blocks?: $provider > [block provider](hitbox.md#block-providers) of the blocks that hide the position, `#bs.hitbox:get_block/collision` by default, as the line of sight of mobs
  output success > whether the entity can see the position

feature function in_view > Check if a position is in the field of view of an entity: a cone around the direction it looks at.
  authors Aksiome, Leirof
  since 2019/05/20 1.20.3
  @executor > entity that looks, from its eyes
  @position > position to check
  input arguments
    angle: number @ 0..180 > angle of the cone in degrees, in the world rather than on screen
  output success > whether the position is in the field of view
